{
	"about": "A case as the server holds it (GET /api/v1/teams/{teamId}/cases/{caseId}) and the case.json of its download (GET …/export) in the extension's format sitegloss/1 (DEC-022). The server's caseFileOf (apps/app/src/server/case-file.ts) gives caseJson for server; the extension's mapping of a server case (mergeCase in src/lib/cloud/wire.ts) has to give the same, and its validateCase has to keep it as it is. Mark 1's element and mark 3's start carry a look (DEC-021), with entries the extension's lookOf drops: a custom property, a value that names a URL, a backdrop's false image and out-of-range depth, a sibling at offset 0. caseMdLookLines: the \"- Look:\" lines the extension's caseMarkdown writes in case.md for caseJson, in order. Screenshot sh_cart has a query (DEC-023): the file's s1 carries it as shots[].query, as the server sends it; sh_pay has none and s2 has no query key. caseMdQueryLines: the lines of case.md that name an address with its query (a mark's \"- Page:\" and the screenshot's \"is of\" line, with the query put back before any hash), in order. singlePageServer, singlePageCaseJson, singlePageCaseMdPageLines: a case with one page and two screenshots of it, sh_results with a query and sh_plain without. The server's caseFileOf gives singlePageCaseJson for singlePageServer, as above. singlePageCaseMdPageLines: every line of its case.md that starts with \"- Page:\" or \"Screenshot \", in order: the case's page, plain; mark 1's page with its screenshot's query; the screenshot with a query and what it is of. Mark 2 and screenshot s2, without a query, name no page, as in a single-page case today (DEC-023).",
